From 838a58e0b969eced928de7ac099999d59b845e94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:47:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] check calls: refuse a replaced carrier's tracking link
 after the load closes

resolveToken only compared the link's carrier with the move's live carrier
assignment while the move was open. Once the move completed or was
canceled the check was skipped, so a carrier replaced mid-load could open
the page again (stops, times, PRO number) for as long as its link lived.

The carrier is now checked whatever the move's status: a closed load still
opens read-only, but only for the carrier that still covers it, and a move
whose carrier coverage was canceled answers like every other dead link.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L7Gd5v8t2y7WHswGwtgbrn
