From 3966de9fe6390efea49e86ae739e7de9d95c645a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:51:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] timesheets: refuse clock-outs and manual hours dated in
 the future

ClockIn refused a punch dated more than a minute ahead, but ClockOut took
any At, so a worker (from the driver portal or the time clock) could close
a punch hours ahead and be paid for time not yet worked, on a sheet a
manager could approve before it happened. RecordEntry had the same gap for
hand-entered periods.

ClockIn, ClockOut and RecordEntry now share one check that refuses a time
more than a minute past now (the clock-skew allowance ClockIn already
used).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L7Gd5v8t2y7WHswGwtgbrn
---
